-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/dbd74663-ce07-5fc8-9faa-2fc96621e839
-- title:
--   Level automorphisms matching two ideals over a supersingular place (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data. Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $\ell_g$ be a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   The valuation ring and the reduction datum. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ belongs to `A.nonunits`. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, and let `hW` say that $W$ consists exactly of the members of `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, of those places $w$ that are rational, satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which the value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen _ M')` lies in `ssJSet q`. Let `hle` assert the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $M'$ into the base change of the function field of $X_{H}(q^2M')$ for $H =$ `levelH q M'`. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees, together with the conditions that an element of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $A$ exactly when its image lies in `R₀.integers`, that `R₀.residue` is compatible with reduction $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ on constants, that every nonzero $f$ admits a scalar $c$ with $c \cdot f$ in `R₀.integers` of nonzero residue, and that divisors of functions with nonzero residue push forward along `R₀.placeMap` to divisors of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires coefficientwise compatibility: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally let $s$ be an element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place in the above sense.
--
--   Local data over a field of constants. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$, write $A_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the valuation subring induced on $k_0$, and let $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lie in $A$. The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` require, respectively, that $A_0$ be a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal be generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ be a Henselian local ring, and that its residue field be algebraically closed. The hypothesis `hκ` requires that every $a \in A$ be congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   Level data. Let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and let `hιξ` provide a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $H_1$ be the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times}$ given by `hH₁` as the intersection of `levelH q M'` — the kernel of the reduction `ZMod.unitsMap` attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'` — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^{\times}$ coming from $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of `LaurentSeries k₀` over $k_0$, required by `hK` to be `laurentBaseChange k₀ (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`, the field generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions forming the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$ over $\mathbb{Q}$; $K$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with the tower $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be an element whose Laurent series is `coeffEmb k₀ jq`, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, and let $j \neq 0$.
--
--   The two ideals and the congruence hypotheses. Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over `Algebra.adjoin A₀ {j}`. Let $y$ and $y'$ be maximal ideals of $C$, both containing the image of $\pi_0$ under $A_0 \to C$. The hypotheses `hover` and `hover'` are of identical shape, for $y$ and for $y'$ respectively: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in `R₀.integers`, subject to (i) at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, nonnegativity of $P.\mathrm{ord}$ on the base change of `jq` implies nonnegativity of $P.\mathrm{ord}$ on the base change of $g$, and (ii) the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$; then, for every proof that `coeffEmb k₀ g` lies in $K$ and that the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals `s.evalAt` applied to the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference in $C$ between that element and the image of $c$ lies in $y$ (respectively in $y'$).
--
--   Conclusion. Under these hypotheses there exist $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$, such that the following three assertions hold.
--
--   First, `IsLevelAutAt k₀ q ξ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`: for every weight $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ of weight $k$ for the group [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), all integral power series $p_f, p_g$ that are integral $q$-expansions of $f$ and of $g$ with `intSeriesC ℚ pg ≠ 0`, every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of `intSeriesC ℚ pf / intSeriesC ℚ pg`, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/q)$, the product of the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the Laurent series of $\tau x$ with the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k$ `conjElemN q γ⁻¹` equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k$ `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`.
--
--   Second, $\tau$ maps $C$ into itself: every $f \in C$ has $\tau f \in C$.
--
--   Third, $\tau$ carries $y$ to $y'$ in the following sense: for every $f \in C$ with $\tau f \in C$, one has $f \in y$ if and only if $\tau f \in y'$.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$, $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-rigidified form of the orbit statement asserting that the maximal ideals of the integral chart of the auxiliary level-$q^2M'$ modular curve lying above a fixed supersingular place $s$ are permuted transitively by the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$, the auxiliary full level being replaced by the diamond condition at the guard prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$. It is used in the construction of the semistable chart data and of the inertia description at the supersingular fibres, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.AuxLevel.exists_mem_invariants_forall_valuationSubring_over_not_mem_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.AuxLevel.exists_mem_invariants_forall_valuationSubring_over_not_mem_of_rigidChart_linkedScalars_of_eq_three_of_dvd) and by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_inertia_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
-- source:
